## Overview: the owner-create pipeline

The create-owner endpoint is defined by the OfficeFloor YAML at `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`. Each step names a Java function class in `src/main/java/.../rest/function/owner/`. The relevant-to-you nodes are `validate` → `rejectDailyLimit` → ... → `build` → `assignNamesakeCount` → `defaultRegistrationDate` → `assignCustomerCode` → `assignHousehold` → `save` → `respond`. The membership number is not stored; it is derived at response time by the mapper.

### 1) The owners.POST.yml pipeline (verbatim)

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`

```yaml
composition:
  authorize: "hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')"

normalizeAddress:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.NormalizeOwnerAddress
  govern: [ transaction ]
  next: validate

validate:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.ValidateRequiredOwnerFields
